id: pm-rl-hncb
title: Certify pm-rl against PM CLI SDK 2026.9.28
description: "Upgrade the candidate development CLI and SDK to published 2026.9.28 to match the active pm-github extension SDK; retain published pm-ops 2026.9.28 and pm-changelog 2026.9.25. Certify direct release gates, packed npm/Bun behavior, and strict tracker health. Companion rollout: pm-cli-website-377e."
type: Chore
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-26T19:59:42.997Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-28T19:57:12.474Z"
author: codex
acceptance_criteria: "Package and lockfile pin published PM CLI 2026.9.28, pm-ops 2026.9.28, pm-changelog 2026.9.25; full direct release:check and strict tracker health pass on installed dependencies; packed npm and Bun extension acceptance is measured; PR links this item and records independent review and recursive-training limitations."
parent: pm-rl-apvf
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-28T06:51:05.996Z",claude-hub,"2026-09-28: pinned pm-ops 2026.9.28 and re-copied its templates/prepare-merge-driver.ts in 29e11d7 (pm-ops#124: the omit-dev skip now checks every Node resolution path for an incomplete hoisted pm-ops). release:check and changelog:check pass on this branch. Acceptance criteria and the launcher link note now name pm-ops 2026.9.28; the dated 2026.9.26 notes above stay as historical results."
notes[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-26T20:06:25.026Z",codex,"Initial pm test linked release gate failed because the default schema sandbox injected PM_PATH into npm tests that initialize their own temporary trackers; direct release:check reached a real canonical-launcher mismatch with pm-ops 2026.9.26. Updated the launcher from the installed canonical template. Both observations are distinct; revalidation follows."
  "2026-09-26T20:15:33.662Z",codex,"2026-09-26: Direct npm run release:check on installed PM CLI/SDK 2026.9.26, pm-ops 2026.9.26 and pm-changelog 2026.9.25 passed 329/329 tests, 0 failures, 100.00% statements/lines/branches/functions over 20 authored source files, 136/136 documented declarations, zero duplication and zero npm production vulnerabilities. Packed pm-rl tarball installed and imported under npm/Node and Bun 1.3.5. PM linked bandit acceptance passed 14/14. Strict PM health ok=true with an existing provenance-value warning. Full linked npm test context limitation is upstream pm-cli#1318; direct full gate is the valid package result."
  "2026-09-26T20:16:50.259Z",codex,"PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/pull/54 proposes the SDK and canonical launcher update. Exact-head CI, bot review, merge and publication remain pending independently of the passed local release gate."
  "2026-09-28T19:51:00.569Z","harness:codex","2026-09-28 red-first CLI 2026.9.28 gate: one real host-bound test failed because pm install pointed at the whole checkout and the current CLI refused an incomplete 10000-entry source scan. Replaced that one-use fixture with npm pack archive installation through pm package install. Focused compiled test passed 1/1. The CLI refusal is expected upstream behavior; this is a package test correction."
  "2026-09-28T19:57:12.452Z","harness:codex","2026-09-28 final local CLI 2026.9.28 candidate: direct release:check passed 329/329 tests with 0 failures or skips. Coverage gate measured 100.00% statements lines branches and functions over 20 authored source files; docstrings 136/136 declarations; duplication zero; production npm audit zero vulnerabilities; package pack and changelog check passed. A red-first host-bound test failed on the now-correct 10000-entry local source scan refusal and passed after installing the packed archive. Fresh npm/Node and Bun 1.3.5 projects imported the tarball and npx/bunx ran pm 2026.9.28. A linked snapshot workspace run of the focused packed mutation test passed 1/1; initial linked none/source and isolated attempts failed on context and absent test file, respectively. Strict PM health passes with one historical provenance advisory. pm-github public issue import and sync dry runs planned zero writes because the repo currently has zero GitHub issues. This does not certify a nonempty import, recursive controller, hosted service or external reviews."
